{"path":"ranges/range_adaptor_closure","title":"std::ranges::range_adaptor_closure","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::</span>range_adaptor_closure","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/range_adaptor_closure","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"std::ranges::range_adaptor_closure is a helper class template for defining a RangeAdaptorClosureObject.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/ranges\">&lt;ranges&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> D <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; requires <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/is_object\"><span class=\"kw494\">std::<span class=\"me2\">is_object_v</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>D<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/same_as\"><span class=\"kw2951\">std::<span class=\"me2\">same_as</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>D, <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/remove_cv\"><span class=\"kw602\">std::<span class=\"me2\">remove_cv_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>D<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span><br><span class=\"kw1\">class</span> range_adaptor_closure <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>std::ranges::range_adaptor_closure</code> is a helper class template for defining a <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/RangeAdaptorClosureObject\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">RangeAdaptorClosureObject</em></a>.\n</p><p>Let <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t</span></code> be the object of type <code>T</code>, the implementation ensures that <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t</span></code> is a range adaptor closure object if all the requirements are met:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">t</span></code> is a unary function object that takes one <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><code>range</code></a> argument.\n</li><li> <code>T</code> has exactly one public base class <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ranges<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">range_adaptor_closure</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span>, and <code>T</code> has no base classes of type <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">ranges<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">range_adaptor_closure</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>U<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span> for any other type <code>U</code>.\n</li><li> <code>T</code> does not satisfy <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range\"><code>range</code></a>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<table class=\"wikitable ftm-begin ftm-has-value\">\n<tr>\n<th><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/feature_test\">Feature-test</a> macro\n</th>\n<th><abbr>Value</abbr>\n</th>\n<th><abbr>Std</abbr>\n</th>\n<th>Feature\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/feature_test#cpp_lib_ranges\"><code>__cpp_lib_ranges</code></a></td>\n<td><a href=\"/w/cpp/compiler_support/23#cpp_lib_ranges_202202L\"><code>202202L</code></a></td>\n<td><span class=\"t-mark\">(C++23)</span></td>\n<td><code>std::ranges::range_adaptor_closure</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ranges&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string_view&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"co1\">// Define Slice as a range adaptor closure</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> Slice <span class=\"sy4\">:</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ranges</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">range_adaptor_closure</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>Slice<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> start <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/types/size_t\"><span class=\"kw107\">std::<span class=\"me2\">size_t</span></span></a> end <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view/npos\"><span class=\"kw1257\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">npos</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> operator<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> sv<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> sv.<span class=\"me1\">substr</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>start, end <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> start<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a> str <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"01234567\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> Slice slicer<span class=\"br0\">{</span>.<span class=\"me1\">start</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, .<span class=\"me1\">end</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// use slicer as a normal function object</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> sv1 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> slicer<span class=\"br0\">(</span>str<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>sv1 <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"12345\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// use slicer as a range adaptor closure object</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> sv2 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> str <span class=\"sy3\">|</span> slicer<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>sv2 <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"12345\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// range adaptor closures can be composed</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> slice_and_drop <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> slicer <span class=\"sy3\">|</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view\"><span class=\"kw2946\">views::<span class=\"me2\">drop</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string_view\"><span class=\"kw1256\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string_view</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>str <span class=\"sy3\">|</span> slice_and_drop<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"345\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::range_adaptor_closure","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++23. std::ranges::range_adaptor_closure is a helper class template for defining a RangeAdaptorClosureObject."},{"label":"Notes"},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++23"],"wordCount":210,"codeBlockCount":1}
